    "findings": [
      {
        "topic": "quantifier order",
        "result": "passed source inspection",
        "details": "For each fixed-label open neighborhood, epsilon and residue depth precede the fixed-source thresholds. Finite label conjunction and Finset.eventually_all yield a single threshold for the fixed finite C before all n, T in C, and actual marks. No growing or infinite source family is uniformly quantified."
      },
      {
        "topic": "original common point",
        "result": "passed source inspection",
        "details": "Both actual marks retain complete source prefixes and exact Parikh equality. The common point is ambientStar of top.before; exact balance rewrites bottom approximation around that same point. Reference witness ordinals are not counted or asserted injective."
      },
      {
        "topic": "fixture and carrier",
        "result": "passed source inspection",
        "details": "Tiles, fixed word, ambientStar, incidence endomorphism and quotient residues retain the same fixture. The existing matrix-adic carrier and topology are consumed directly."
      },
      {
        "topic": "strict labels",
        "result": "passed source inspection",
        "details": "Generic distinct-cut statements assume distinct labels explicitly. The strict-carrier theorem derives them from the supplied actual StrictSystem via strict_cut_labels; no strict system is constructed."
      },
      {
        "topic": "finite open cover",
        "result": "passed source inspection",
        "details": "overlapUnion_compact supplies a finite subcover J first. The eventual cut theorem is then applied to its open union to select N. The cover is not assumed to be an arbitrary measurable or half-open cover."
      },
      {
        "topic": "scope boundaries",
        "result": "passed source inspection",
        "details": "The empty-overlap theorem remains conditional. No exact intersection membership, lattice count, Haar normalization, density, positive measure, PDS or PSC theorem is inferred."
      }
    ],
